MyDNS for Debian (MySQL/MariaDB backend)
========================================

The service is installed and enabled but not started, because it needs a
database first.

1. Create the database and a user for mydns:

     mysql -e "CREATE DATABASE mydns;
               CREATE USER mydns@localhost IDENTIFIED BY 'secret';
               GRANT SELECT ON mydns.* TO mydns@localhost;"

   Grant INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE as well if you enable DNS UPDATE.

2. Create the tables:

     mydns --create-tables | mysql mydns

   For long or multi-string TXT records, widen rr.data:

     mysql mydns -e "ALTER TABLE rr MODIFY data VARBINARY(1024) NOT NULL"

3. Put the credentials into /etc/mydns.conf (mode 0600, root only: mydns
   reads it before dropping privileges to the _mydns user).

4. Start it:

     systemctl start mydns

Logs go to syslog (the journal): journalctl -u mydns
